  "title": "Not All Jurisdictions are Created Equal",
  "summary": "This episode of Athene: In Context takes us offshore, where Mike Downing and John Golden draw a clear distinction between Bermuda, the largest offshore reinsurance jurisdiction in the world, with capital, transparency, and governance standards consistent with those of the U.S., and the Cayman Islands, where a \"choose your own adventure\" approach to capital and regulation is creating contagion risk.",
